Bug: Extract function drops the declaration of locals returned through out parameters

When the region declares two locals that the code after it uses, they come back
through out parameters, but the call site no longer declares them:
`newFunction_(text, textSize, &spaces, &tabs);` without `int spaces, tabs;`
before it. With one such local it works, since it is returned and declared at the
call site (tests/test_extract_local_declared_in_region_used_after).

The fix is to emit the declarations at the call site before the call, without
initialisers, since the function sets them. Workaround until then: leave the
declarations out of the region.

GitHub issue #79.
